{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"SUPERSEDED by eb58-e71d-ec90-4b00 (Model classes: trivial/standard/frontier). This ticket proposed a per-provider mapping and a minimal verifier knob; the operator-approved design instead makes three capability CLASSES the universal interface, which subsumes this ticket's whole contract and removes the need for a short-lived REBAR_LLM_VERIFIER_MODEL surface. All of this ticket's findings carry forward as acceptance criteria on eb58's children: the three inverted verifier paths (verify.py:269, completion.py:332, code-review's missing downgrade) are 172e-b207-4c18-4243, and the bare-ladder split-brain is 7761-4b1a-e8c3-45a0. Nothing is lost; the mechanism changed."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785470800933445001,"uuid":"58a76650-9594-4521-bf5d-419421b9c0d9"}